From 8adbfcb72f293fd8331c2344bbcbf302401d2806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian <219239532+markd3ng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 20:40:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(paste): consume max-reads before returning the body
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Context:
Issue #84 (C Max reads ADOPT_WITH_REDESIGN) requires an optional
race-safe burn-after-read limit. KV cannot increment atomically, so
a per-paste Durable Object serializes consume-before-response.

This commit is the replay adaptation of accepted source HEAD
7540a3cad785404463cab71a071deebad50081b7 onto assembled 010–120.
Source PR #115 is not rewritten.

Expected behavior:
Form field r stores maxReads plus a new readStateVersion. Content
GETs (raw, /a/, /u/) load the paste, consume, then return the body
with Cache-Control: no-store, or 404 with no body if exhausted. The
last successful consume deletes the paste via waitUntil. HEAD, /m/,
and /d/ do not consume. /d/ skips SSR when maxReads is set. PUT
without r clears the limit; PUT with r rotates readStateVersion.
Unlimited pastes never touch the Durable Object. Patch 110 Range is
disabled whenever maxReads is set.

Acceptance criteria:
- r=1: first content GET 200, second 404
- r=2: two 200 then 404
- invalid r is 400
- concurrent r=1 content GETs are one 200 and one 404
- HEAD and /m/ do not consume
- /a/ and /u/ consume; /d/ skips __PASTE_DATA__ and does not consume
- PUT without r restores unlimited reads
- PUT with r starts a new counter
- Range on a read-limited paste is ignored (200, not 206) and still
  consumes once

Constraints:
- Replay-adapted onto assembled 010–120. Do not merge into upstream-sync.
- Residual: losing concurrent request may load bytes into the isolate
  before DO reject; those bytes are not returned.

Replay adaptation (source branch not rewritten):
- README.md: keep Patch 110 encrypted-Display-download bullet and
  Patch 120 ZIP bullet; add Patch 130 max-reads bullet.
- shared/constants.ts: keep Patch 060 MPU headers and Patch 070
  DEFAULT_EDIT_FILENAME; add MAX_READS_CAP.
- shared/verify.ts: keep Patch 010 parseExpirationSpec / 030
  isLegalRedirectUrl; add parseMaxReads.
- worker/handlers/handleWrite.ts: keep Patch 010 expiration spec,
  Patch 050 named create, and Patch 070 filename helper; add r.
- worker/handlers/handleRead.ts: keep Patch 110 Range helpers;
  pasteAllowsByteRange already rejects maxReads.
- worker/storage/storage.ts: keep schemaVersion 2, null expiration,
  and mimeType; add maxReads / readStateVersion.
- worker/test/maxReads.spec.ts: add assembled /u/ consume and
  Range-off coverage.

